{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>For YHWH is with him</b> — the name of Heaven was fluent in his mouth; this is the language of Rashi (Rashi on Genesis 39:3). But this does not seem correct. Rather, \"his master saw that YHWH was with him\" means that his deeds succeeded at all times more than those of any other man, and he knew that it was from Elohim that he had it. And likewise (Genesis 26:28), \"We saw plainly that YHWH was with you.\" And he found favor in his eyes, and he appointed him his personal attendant and put him in charge of his household."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 39, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:41:49.962286098Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}